From 00ac767a00e8c2dc2b3b478ce1961156b8df9ec9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 17:00:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Check the multicast join over N2 in MBS-MC-02

Replace the MBS-MC-02 stub with a check of the signalling half of the
requirement, decided from an N2 capture like MBS-BC-07 is: that the AMF
activated the multicast session in the gNB and the gNB accepted it, that the
two joining UEs' PDU sessions were associated with that MBS session and the
gNB accepted that too, and that the third UE got none of it.

The radio half -- a multicast MRB for each member, and payload arriving -- is
reported as not implemented in a section of its own, with what it needs.

A join names a TMGI, and the TMGI is whatever the core allocates, so the
session is created first and ue1 and ue2 are then restarted with
--mbs-join <tmgi>. MBS_UE1_EXTRA / MBS_UE2_EXTRA / MBS_UE3_EXTRA in the
compose file append options to one UE's command line, which is what makes
"ue1 and ue2 join, ue3 does not" expressible.

decode_ngap.py gains what the check needs:

- the TMGI is looked for inside the nested *Transfer octet strings, not only
  at the top level -- the MBS session of a per-UE PDU Session Resource Modify
  lives inside pDUSessionResourceModifyRequestTransfer;
- the RAN UE NGAP ID is reported, which is the only thing in a capture that
  tells one UE's procedures from another's, with --ran-ue to filter by it.
  Finding it needed the search to understand pycrate's CHOICE pairs, since an
  open-type IE value is a CHOICE and RAN-UE-NGAP-ID is its name, not a key.

tests/tools/test_decode_ngap.py is a self-test of the decoder that needs no
testbed: it builds the PDUs the MBS checks read with the same pycrate grammar,
writes them into a capture and decodes them back, including the negative case
of a UE that appears on N2 with no MBS procedure.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
