 *Multicast · R-SYS-5011, R-SYS-5031, R-SYS-5034, R-SYS-5036*
 
-Where membership starts to mean something. A `MULTICAST` session is created
-and activated, two of the three UEs join, and both receive — each having
-been given a multicast MRB by RRC reconfiguration.
+Where membership starts to mean something. A `MULTICAST` session is created,
+two of the three UEs join it, and the core and the RAN agree about who is in
+it — decided from a capture of N2, for the same reason MBS-BC-07 is: a log
+line says what a process believes, a capture says what crossed the interface.
+
+What this asserts is the **signalling** half of the requirement: that the AMF
+activated the session in the gNB and the gNB accepted it, that each joining
+UE's PDU session was associated with that MBS session and the gNB accepted
+that too, and that the UE which did not ask got none of it. The radio half —
+a multicast MRB for each member, and payload arriving — is reported separately
+below, still unimplemented.
+
+A join needs a TMGI, and the TMGI is whatever the core allocates, so the
+session is created first and the two joining UEs are then restarted with
+`--mbs-join <tmgi>`. `MBS_UE1_EXTRA` and `MBS_UE2_EXTRA` in the compose file
+exist for exactly this: one UE gets an option the others do not.
 
-<details><summary>the verdict</summary>
+<details><summary>start capturing N2 at the gNB, before the session exists</summary>
+
+Same arrangement as MBS-BC-07: a container sharing the gNB's network, writing
+into a fresh `mktemp -d` because tcpdump writes the file as root.
+
+```sh {"name":"mc02-capture-start"}
+set -eu
+export MBS_MC_N2DIR=$(mktemp -d)
+docker rm -f mbs-n2cap >/dev/null 2>&1 || true
+docker run -d --name mbs-n2cap --network container:gnb -v "$MBS_MC_N2DIR":/cap \
+  --entrypoint tcpdump "${PHINE_UE_IMAGE:-phine_oai_ue:ptm}" -i eth0 -nn -s0 -U -w /cap/n2.pcap sctp >/dev/null
+sleep 2
+echo "capturing N2 next to gnb"
+```
+
+</details>
+
+Create the session. Same request as the broadcast one, with
+`"serviceType":"MULTICAST"`.
+
+```sh {"name":"mc02-session"}
+docker exec core curl -s --http2-prior-knowledge -X POST \
+  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
+  -d '{"mbsSession":{"ssm":{"sourceIpAddr":{"ipv4Addr":"192.168.77.20"},
+       "destIpAddr":{"ipv4Addr":"239.0.0.26"}},"tmgiAllocReq":true,
+       "serviceType":"MULTICAST","snssai":{"sst":1},
+       "mbsServiceArea":{"tais":[{"plmnId":{"mcc":"999","mnc":"70"},"tac":"000001"}]}}}' \
+  127.0.0.4:7777/nmbsmf-mbssession/v1/mbs-sessions | tee /tmp/mbs-mc-session.json
+echo
+```
+
+<details><summary>work out the TMGI the core allocated, as the UEs have to name it</summary>
+
+The TMGI on the wire is six octets: three of MBS Service ID then the PLMN, in
+the TS 24.008 encoding (999/70 is `99 f9 07`). The API reports the service ID
+and the PLMN separately, so they are put together here — and the same string
+is what `--mbs-join` takes and what the capture is searched for, so a mistake
+shows up as a failed assertion rather than as a silent mismatch.
+
+```sh {"name":"mc02-tmgi"}
+set -eu
+export MBS_MC_SID=$(grep -o '"mbsServiceId":"[^"]*"' /tmp/mbs-mc-session.json | head -1 | cut -d'"' -f4 | tr 'A-F' 'a-f' || true)
+[ -n "${MBS_MC_SID:-}" ] || { echo "FAIL: the core did not report an mbsServiceId"; cat /tmp/mbs-mc-session.json; exit 1; }
+export MBS_MC_TMGI=$(python3 -c "
+import json, sys
+s = json.load(open('/tmp/mbs-mc-session.json'))
+tmgi = (s.get('mbsSession') or s).get('tmgi') or {}
+plmn = tmgi.get('plmnId') or {}
+mcc, mnc = plmn.get('mcc', '999'), plmn.get('mnc', '70')
+# TS 24.008 10.5.6.13: MCC digit 2|1, MNC digit 3|MCC digit 3, MNC digit 2|1,
+# with 'f' for the third MNC digit of a two-digit MNC.
+mnc3 = mnc[2] if len(mnc) == 3 else 'f'
+print('%s%s%s%s%s%s%s' % ('$MBS_MC_SID', mcc[1], mcc[0], mnc3, mcc[2], mnc[1], mnc[0]))
+")
+echo "the core allocated TMGI $MBS_MC_TMGI (service id $MBS_MC_SID)"
+```
+
+</details>
+
+ue1 and ue2 join it. ue3 is left alone.
+
+```sh {"name":"mc02-join"}
+cd "$MBS_A_DIR"
+MBS_UE1_EXTRA="--mbs-join $MBS_MC_TMGI" docker compose up -d --force-recreate ue1
+MBS_UE2_EXTRA="--mbs-join $MBS_MC_TMGI" docker compose up -d --force-recreate ue2
+```
+
+<details><summary>wait for the two of them to attach again, then let the join finish</summary>
+
+The join is sent once the UE's PDU session is up, so the attach has to be
+waited for; the extra seconds after it are for the NAS exchange and the two N2
+procedures it causes.
+
+```sh {"name":"mc02-wait"}
+set -eu
+for n in 1 2; do
+  echo -n "waiting for ue$n"
+  for i in $(seq 90); do
+    docker exec ue$n ip -4 addr show oaitun_ue1 2>/dev/null | grep 'inet ' >/dev/null && break
+    echo -n .; sleep 1
+  done
+  docker exec ue$n ip -4 addr show oaitun_ue1 2>/dev/null | grep 'inet ' >/dev/null \
+    || { echo " FAIL: ue$n did not attach"; docker logs ue$n 2>&1 | tail -10; exit 1; }
+  echo " attached"
+done
+sleep 8
+```
+
+</details>
+
+<details><summary>stop the capture, decode N2, and decide</summary>
+
+Four things are asserted, all from the capture:
+
+* the AMF sent a Multicast Session Activation (procedure code 71) naming the
+  TMGI the core allocated, and the gNB answered it with a `successfulOutcome`.
+  A `unsuccessfulOutcome` is a failure here, not an absence;
+* two distinct UEs got a PDU Session Resource Modify (procedure code 26)
+  carrying that same TMGI — that is the join reaching the RAN, one UE at a
+  time. The UEs are told apart by RAN UE NGAP ID, which is the only thing in a
+  capture that distinguishes them;
+* each of those two UEs answered with a `successfulOutcome` carrying the TMGI;
+* no third UE appears in either list. ue3 attached and has a PDU session like
+  the others, so an MBS procedure naming it would mean the core sent the join
+  to every UE rather than to the ones that asked — which is the failure this
+  check exists to catch.
+
+`decode_ngap.py` reports the TMGI of a per-UE modify by decoding the nested
+`pDUSessionResourceModifyRequestTransfer`, which is an opaque octet string at
+the top level of the PDU.
 
 ```sh {"name":"mc02-verify"}
 set -eu
-echo "MBS-MC-02 NOT IMPLEMENTED: multicast sessions are not supported."
-echo "  would check: NGAP multicast session setup and activation; ue1 and"
-echo "               ue2 send MBSInterestIndication and are given a"
-echo "               multicast MRB by RRC reconfiguration; both receive"
-echo "               (R-SYS-5011, R-SYS-5031, R-SYS-5034, R-SYS-5036)"
-echo "  needs:       Milestone 2 -- multicast session type, join signalling,"
-echo "               per-session membership state"
-export MBS_RESULTS="${MBS_RESULTS:-}NOTIMPL multicast MBS-MC-02;"
+cd "$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)"
+sleep 3
+docker rm -f mbs-n2cap >/dev/null 2>&1 || true
+
+BAD=0
+python3 tests/tools/decode_ngap.py "$MBS_MC_N2DIR/n2.pcap" --procedure-code 71 | tee /tmp/n2-71.txt || true
+python3 tests/tools/decode_ngap.py "$MBS_MC_N2DIR/n2.pcap" --procedure-code 26 | tee /tmp/n2-26.txt || true
+
+ACT_REQ=$(grep initiatingMessage /tmp/n2-71.txt | grep -c "tmgi=$MBS_MC_TMGI" || true)
+ACT_OK=$(grep successfulOutcome /tmp/n2-71.txt | grep -c "tmgi=$MBS_MC_TMGI" || true)
+ACT_FAIL=$(grep -c unsuccessfulOutcome /tmp/n2-71.txt || true)
+[ "$ACT_REQ" -ge 1 ] && echo "ok: the AMF asked the gNB to activate TMGI $MBS_MC_TMGI" \
+                     || { echo "FAIL: no Multicast Session Activation for $MBS_MC_TMGI on N2"; BAD=1; }
+[ "$ACT_OK" -ge 1 ] && echo "ok: the gNB answered the activation successfully" \
+                    || { echo "FAIL: the gNB did not answer the activation"; BAD=1; }
+[ "$ACT_FAIL" -eq 0 ] || { echo "FAIL: the gNB answered the activation with a failure"; BAD=1; }
+
+# The joining UEs, by RAN UE NGAP ID, from the modify requests that name the TMGI.
+JOINED=$(grep initiatingMessage /tmp/n2-26.txt | grep "tmgi=$MBS_MC_TMGI" \
+         | grep -oE 'ran_ue=[0-9]+' | cut -d= -f2 | sort -u || true)
+ANSWERED=$(grep successfulOutcome /tmp/n2-26.txt | grep "tmgi=$MBS_MC_TMGI" \
+           | grep -oE 'ran_ue=[0-9]+' | cut -d= -f2 | sort -u || true)
+N_JOINED=$(echo "$JOINED" | grep -c . || true)
+N_ANSWERED=$(echo "$ANSWERED" | grep -c . || true)
+
+echo "UEs the core associated with the session: ${JOINED:-none}"
+echo "UEs the gNB confirmed:                    ${ANSWERED:-none}"
+
+[ "$N_JOINED" -eq 2 ] && echo "ok: exactly two UEs were associated with the MBS session" \
+                      || { echo "FAIL: $N_JOINED UE(s) were associated, expected 2 (ue1 and ue2)"; BAD=1; }
+[ "$N_ANSWERED" -eq 2 ] && echo "ok: the gNB accepted both of them" \
+                        || { echo "FAIL: the gNB confirmed $N_ANSWERED of them, expected 2"; BAD=1; }
+if [ "$N_JOINED" -eq 2 ] && [ "$N_ANSWERED" -eq 2 ]; then
+  [ "$JOINED" = "$ANSWERED" ] && echo "ok: the gNB confirmed the same two UEs the core named" \
+                              || { echo "FAIL: the core named [$JOINED], the gNB confirmed [$ANSWERED]"; BAD=1; }
+fi
+
+if [ "$BAD" -eq 0 ]; then
+  echo "MBS-MC-02 passed (signalling; the radio part is below)"
+  export MBS_RESULTS="${MBS_RESULTS:-}PASS multicast MBS-MC-02;"
+else
+  echo "MBS-MC-02 FAILED"
+  export MBS_RESULTS="${MBS_RESULTS:-}FAIL multicast MBS-MC-02;"
+fi
+```
+
+</details>
+
+<details><summary>the radio part, still unimplemented</summary>
+
+The signalling above says the gNB knows which UEs joined. Turning that into
+reception needs the parts tonight's work deliberately left out, so it is
+reported rather than asserted — a check that cannot pass yet should be visible,
+not absent.
+
+```sh {"name":"mc02-radio"}
+set -eu
+echo "MBS-MC-02 radio NOT IMPLEMENTED: the joined UEs get no multicast MRB."
+echo "  would check: ue1 and ue2 are given a multicast MRB by RRC"
+echo "               reconfiguration and both receive on 239.0.0.26, ue3"
+echo "               receives nothing (R-SYS-5031, R-SYS-5034, R-SYS-5036)"
+echo "  needs:       Distribution Setup so the shared NG-U tunnel exists;"
+echo "               then the multicast MRB and DCI 4_2 scheduling"
+export MBS_RESULTS="${MBS_RESULTS:-}NOTIMPL multicast MBS-MC-02-radio;"
 ```
 
 </details>
